# Free language-model keys for the in-app assistant.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.llm` (same folder), fill in the keys you have, and
# run:
#
#   .\tools\setup_ai_assistant.ps1
#
# The file is ignored by git, so the keys stay on this machine. Every provider
# you fill in is switched on; the edge function tries them in order and moves
# to the next one when the first is rate-limited or down.
#
# All three are free to start with and speak the OpenAI protocol:
#
#   GROQ_API_KEY        from https://console.groq.com/keys
#                       Groq free plan: 30 requests a minute, 1000 a day.
#
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY  from https://openrouter.ai/keys
#                       OpenRouter free models: about 200 requests a day.
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY      from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#                       Google AI Studio free tier.
#
# The models are optional: the defaults are open-weight models that are free
# on every one of the three. Set them only to pin a different one.

GROQ_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/free
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
